hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16689","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from al-Walid ibn al-Walid that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I feel loneliness. He said: When you take your bed, say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His anger, His punishment, the evil of His servants, the whisperings of the devils, and that they attend me. For it shall not harm, and it is likely none shall approach you."
"24340","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from al-Walid ibn al-Walid, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I feel loneliness, he said: When you take your bed, say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His anger and punishment, and the evil of His servants, and the whispers of the devils, and that they attend me, for it will not harm you, and it is likely none will come near you."
